

what common commands actually prove:

Command

Question you’re answering


show version

Did device reboot? What platform/software?


show ip int brief

Which L3 interfaces are operational?


show interfaces X

What is happening physically/operationally on X?


show run interface X

What is X configured to do?


show logging

What happened and in what order?


show ip arp

Which IPv4-to-MAC mappings does this device know?


show mac address-table

Where did the switch learn MAC addresses?


show vlan brief

Which VLANs exist locally?


show interfaces trunk

Which links trunk and which VLANs cross them?


show spanning-tree

What L2 topology has STP selected?


show etherchannel summary

Are bundle members actually participating?


show cdp neighbors detail

What network device is connected where?


show ip route

Which L3 paths are installed?


show ip bgp summary

Are BGP sessions established?


show ip bgp

What does BGP know?


show ip ospf neighbor

Are OSPF adjacencies healthy?


show ip pim neighbor

Are directly connected PIM routers present?


show ip mroute

What multicast forwarding state exists?


show controllers

What does the underlying hardware/controller see?


ping

Can packets reach and return from this target?


traceroute

Approximately how far does the path progress?

